== Error Description ==
Object storage uploads failing with TLS/SSL certificate errors since 2024-03-15.

== Error Messages ==
$ aws s3 cp large-file.bin s3://company-backup-bucket/
SSL validation failed for https://company-backup-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/large-file.bin
[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: certificate has expired (_ssl.c:1129)

$ curl -v https://s3.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/
* Connected to s3.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com
* SSL certificate verify fail: certificate has expired
* Closing connection
curl: (60) SSL certificate problem: certificate has expired

== Certificate Details ==
openssl s_client -connect s3.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com:443 </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -E "notBefore|notAfter|verify"
verify error:num=10:certificate has expired
notBefore=Jan  1 00:00:00 2023 GMT
notAfter=Mar 14 00:00:00 2024 GMT
verify return:1

== System Info ==
OS: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
Python: 3.10.12
certifi: 2022.12.7  (outdated!)
boto3: 1.26.0
AWS CLI: 2.13.0

== Impact ==
- All HTTPS connections to S3 endpoints failing
- Affects 3 applications connecting to multiple buckets
- Started failing after March 15 2024 when cert notAfter date passed
